{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e","id":805450,"title":"How do Werewolves deal with Killing Blows? [2E]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-10T13:41:40-08:00","id":805450,"title":"How do Werewolves deal with Killing Blows? [2E]","content":"What it says on the tin, I'm wondering how werewolves would deal with blows that would kill anyone in an instant, like being shot in the head (or more precisely, the brain), having their heart ripped out, or being decapitated. Now, the 2E core states that anything that would deal aggravated damage to a mortal only deals lethal damage to a werewolf, which technically includes Killing Blows.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't make much sense to me. I mean sure, werewolves have incredible regeneration, but they don't regenerate after they're dead. I can see some instances of Killing Blows not killing werewolves, such as being shot/stabbed in the liver or major bleeding, but how can a werewolf come back from a bullet through the brain?<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm missing something here, would anyone like to clarify, please? Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T13:49:06-08:00","id":805454,"title":"","content":"They're part spirit. Their minds aren't reliant on their brain being in one piece to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T13:50:27-08:00","id":805457,"title":"","content":"Are you talking about the Killing Blow maneuver? It doesn't do aggravated damage, it does automatic lethal damage equal to the full dice pool + the weapon modifier. Often that will wrap around to aggravated damage, but werewolves can't reduce agg caused by lethal wrap around.<br /> <br /> If you're just talking about damage that would logically kill in one hit... Don't narrate hits that way unless they deal enough damage to kill the target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T13:51:22-08:00","id":805458,"title":"","content":"People don't always die from a bullet through the brain, and a werewolf's regeneration would give them much better odds at survival.<br /> <br /> But, mechanically, if you manage to fill up a character's health boxes with Lethal, and they don't get medical or magical attention, or their boxes are full of aggravated damage, such as with a blow that leaves a large hole where a chest and internal organs would be, you'd have yourself a dead werewolf.<br /> <br /> The idea being that an attack that rips out a heart would be one that succeeded on enough to kill said werewolf. Not just, I have 1 Brawl and 3 Strength and I try to rip their heart out and if I get a 1 I succeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T14:20:38-08:00","id":805483,"title":"","content":"Let's also remember of how much damage we look over in normal fight situation. Our typical werewolf will have 7 Health in Hishu ( Human ) Form. Let's say he is ambushed by moderately experienced enemy with the gun - Dexterity 3 + Firearms 3. The attacker making Killing Blow is also using <i>Colt M1911A1</i> (.45 ACP), typical Heavy Pistol weapon - it's making 2 Damage. That mean that our werewolf attacker is making 8 Auto Damage on his Killing Blow ( Dexterity + Firearms Dice Pool and Weapon Damage ). This mean our Uratha now have 1 Aggravated + 6 Lethal wounds.<br /> <br /> So he is long till dead. Especially as at the start of his round he goes straight in to Death Rage, change in to Gauru, and regenerate all the Lethal wounds. On the start of the next round he just have 1 Aggravated, and that's all. Oh, it would be, if we do not count our piss of Gauru that will now tir apart the once werewolf attacker - but it's now other problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Logically looking, only way you can kill werewolf in non-silver using way in one hit is cutting their head off - and I'm still not sure if they will just not regenerate one later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:01:08-08:00","id":805515,"title":"","content":"Everyone knows if you chop off a werewolf's head, the severed head grows a new body, and the beheaded body grows a new head. Now you've got two pissed of werewolves to deal with for your trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:12:18-08:00","id":805523,"title":"","content":"In first edition it was suggested that each of a werewolf's forms exists in a sort of intangible form when they aren't using it, so if that's still true every werewolf has four spare brains to use if one is out of commission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:23:21-08:00","id":805535,"title":"","content":"Thematically there is very little werewolves can't regenerate. They even heal tilts when they heal the associated wound levels so they're nearly impossible to blind, arm wrack, etc in gauru unless you have a silver weapon or are really pouring the pain on to push their health track into agg with lethal damage. Blood of the Wolf, a 1e book, specified as well that even massive organ damage isn't instantly fatal. Heart ripped out, brain blown to pieces with a bullet... they're part spirit and can heal so long as they have Essence remaining to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:29:17-08:00","id":805540,"title":"","content":"IIRC the book says even <i>aggravated</i> can't permanently disable a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Edit: I recalled correctly. Page 94.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 01-10-2016, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:58:52-08:00","id":805561,"title":"","content":"Some know the legends of the Gift of Healing, and the one werewolf who mastered it, to his own regret. The slightest drop of blood shed would grow into fully formed duplicates of himself.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://1.bp.blogspot.com/-wTYYfARYq6I/VhSJ--SSjXI/AAAAAAAQ5JI/Iz9ofKOnkUA/s1600/9_14.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Unfortunately he was a bit of an asshole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T16:03:44-08:00","id":805562,"title":"","content":"It's pretty much as Charlaquin says, don't narrate instant kills unless the attack actually does enough damage to kill the target. <br /> <br /> Also, I just noticed this as I started looking through the books, but do people not automatically fall unconscious after having their rightmost health box filled with lethal anymore? In 1e core it said that being full of lethal makes you comatose, but I find that not being the case in 2es core. Am I missing something or has that actually changed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T16:19:09-08:00","id":805571,"title":"","content":"In both editions, when your rightmost box has Bashing, you have to make a Stamina roll to stay conscious whenever you try to do anything. When you are full of Lethal, you would take another point of damage every minute, giving people time to get you medical attention or stabilize you some other way.<br /> <br /> The regeneration probably help a lot towards keeping you from falling unconscious, or at least staying that way, and one can use Essence to stabilize yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-10-2016, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T23:48:53-08:00","id":805847,"title":"","content":"I do not know if Uratha ever really go unconscious - when they are in last 3 Health box are it's common Kuruth Trigger, so more often than not, they go in to Gauru and rip you in to. And if not in first turn, when they fall unconscious, the next turn is second time they can go in Death Rage - I maybe misremember corebook wording, but I read it as <b>they roll <i>even</i> if they are </b><b>unconscious</b><i>.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T00:23:32-08:00","id":805862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=805847#post805847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when they are in last 3 Health box are it's common Kuruth Trigger</div> </div> </div> </div>No it isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T00:57:05-08:00","id":805878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e#post805450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that doesn't make much sense to me. I mean sure, werewolves have incredible regeneration, but they don't regenerate after they're dead. I can see some instances of Killing Blows not killing werewolves, such as being shot/stabbed in the liver or major bleeding, but how can a werewolf come back from a bullet through the brain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even among humans Traumatic Brain Injury resulting from penetrating head wounds only has a 50% mortality rate, most of those deaths are due to later complications relating to swelling of the brain due to internal bleeding.<br /> <br /> Now in CofD that would be represented by the character suffering sufficient lethal to wrap around to aggravated damage, then bleeding out due to a lack of (or failed) medical attention. A sufficiently powerful round (such as perhaps a .50 rifle round) would be able to completely destroy a brain and kill someone more or less instantly, but that's represented by inflicting sufficient lethal to wrap around and completely fill the health boxes with aggravated.<br /> <br /> I agree with the comments above that you should be careful to describe injuries as matching the amount of damage inflicted, but just remember also that headshots are not quite so lethal in the real world as they are in the movies. This is demonstrated pretty clearly by the way that armies which train to perform headshots (known as the Mozambique drill), teach you to shoot the target twice in the head, then once in the chest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:58:43-08:00","id":806298,"title":"","content":"So, to kill an average Werewolf instantly you need to deal 24 lethal damage in a single action. Pretty hard to execute. Even in a sitting duck situation, allowing for automatic successes, dice pools do not reach 24 dice. Most weapons add +2 damage, which still would require 22 dice. Willpower works on killing blows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:46:47-08:00","id":806345,"title":"","content":"Get more people to strike the killing blow instead of twinking out a single PC for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:46:53-08:00","id":806346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=806298#post806298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to kill an average Werewolf instantly you need to deal 24 lethal damage in a single action.</div> </div> </div> </div>14.<br /> <br /> 7 to fill up Lethal, 7 to wrap around Aggravated.<br /> <br /> Or just 7 if you have a pretty pure silver weapon, like a sword or bullet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-11-2016, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:14:49-08:00","id":806391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=806345#post806345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get more people to strike the killing blow instead of twinking out a single PC for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feels kind of lame to set up an execution scene with two guys and two weapons just for dicepools. Really, if one pistol can't put down a sitting duck werewolf for good, two won't do the trick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=806345#post806345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">14.<br /> <br /> 7 to fill up Lethal, 7 to wrap around Aggravated.<br /> <br /> Or just 7 if you have a pretty pure silver weapon, like a sword or bullet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the impression that even though the human form has only 7 health, changing to Gauru is reflexive in a Kuruth situation. We can argue if death is a Kuruth situation, but by reading the book, I feel like it is. I'm gonna try to find if there is a mention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:25:19-08:00","id":806404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=806391#post806391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feels kind of lame to set up an execution scene with two guys and two weapons just for dicepools. Really, if one pistol can't put down a sitting duck werewolf for good, two won't do the trick.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have the impression that even though the human form has only 7 health, changing to Gauru is reflexive in a Kuruth situation. We can argue if death is a Kuruth situation, but by reading the book, I feel like it is. I'm gonna try to find if there is a mention.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's an execution scene, why do you care about health levels? Double tap the mofo.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:27:53-08:00","id":806410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=806404#post806404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's an execution scene, why do you care about health levels? Double tap the mofo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T15:41:27-08:00","id":806531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=805454#post805454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're part spirit. Their minds aren't reliant on their brain being in one piece to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't make any thematic sense. Werewolves are creatures of duality, thus they need both spirit and flesh to survive. One goes down the other goes down with it, that sort of thing. At least, that's the impression I got from reading Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=805457#post805457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you talking about the Killing Blow maneuver? It doesn't do aggravated damage, it does automatic lethal damage equal to the full dice pool + the weapon modifier. Often that will wrap around to aggravated damage, but werewolves can't reduce agg caused by lethal wrap around.<br /> <br /> If you're just talking about damage that would logically kill in one hit... Don't narrate hits that way unless they deal enough damage to kill the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I thought Killing Blows did aggravated damage equal to the dice pool. Looks like I'm mistaken on that one. The narrative part of the question still stands, though. I mean, the 2E core has this to say on page 9: &quot;Silver is the best way to kill us, but it's not the only way. Sure, we heal really fast \u2014 but we need to get hurt to have something to heal from, and enough of that hurt will kill us as easily as it would anyone else.&quot;<br /> <br /> So clearly werewolves aren't invincible and are living creatures, so vital organ failure should be deadly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nickpire84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=805535#post805535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thematically there is very little werewolves can't regenerate. They even heal tilts when they heal the associated wound levels so they're nearly impossible to blind, arm wrack, etc in gauru unless you have a silver weapon or are really pouring the pain on to push their health track into agg with lethal damage. Blood of the Wolf, a 1e book, specified as well that even massive organ damage isn't instantly fatal. Heart ripped out, brain blown to pieces with a bullet... they're part spirit and can heal so long as they have Essence remaining to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=805878#post805878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even among humans Traumatic Brain Injury resulting from penetrating head wounds only has a 50% mortality rate, most of those deaths are due to later complications relating to swelling of the brain due to internal bleeding.<br /> <br /> Now in CofD that would be represented by the character suffering sufficient lethal to wrap around to aggravated damage, then bleeding out due to a lack of (or failed) medical attention. A sufficiently powerful round (such as perhaps a .50 rifle round) would be able to completely destroy a brain and kill someone more or less instantly, but that's represented by inflicting sufficient lethal to wrap around and completely fill the health boxes with aggravated.<br /> <br /> I agree with the comments above that you should be careful to describe injuries as matching the amount of damage inflicted, but just remember also that headshots are not quite so lethal in the real world as they are in the movies. This is demonstrated pretty clearly by the way that armies which train to perform headshots (known as the Mozambique drill), teach you to shoot the target twice in the head, then once in the chest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so if a werewolf were to get shot in the head or something just as deadly to a human, while in most cases it would bring them up to full lethal, they could heal it in time if they have the Essence to do it. Alright, that makes sense, but what about decapitation? For starters, decapitating a monster to kill it is a common trope, so there's no narrative reason that it shouldn't work with werewolves (that I can see anyway). Second, it should also work on a logical level because even if a werewolf could regenerate full organs, I highly doubt they could do so in time, even with Essence.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, this is assuming that the decapitation is successful and I'm not really looking at the mechanics anymore, considering I was wrong about Killing Blows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T16:30:01-08:00","id":806557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=806531#post806531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't make any thematic sense. Werewolves are creatures of duality, thus they need both spirit and flesh to survive. One goes down the other goes down with it, that sort of thing. At least, that's the impression I got from reading Forsaken.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's true long-term, beast and machine-riding facets aside, but in short term one half can take the burden long enough for the other to repair itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T16:30:21-08:00","id":806558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=806531#post806531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but what about decapitation? For starters, decapitating a monster to kill it is a common trope, so there's no narrative reason that it shouldn't work with werewolves (that I can see anyway). Second, it should also work on a logical level because even if a werewolf could regenerate full organs, I highly doubt they could do so in time, even with Essence.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, this is assuming that the decapitation is successful and I'm not really looking at the mechanics anymore, considering I was wrong about Killing Blows.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Werewolf is restrained to a guillotine and has no means to escape (blocked transformations or something of the sort), he is pretty much dead. He is not capable of surviving without his entire head. However, this should be a scene designed specially, there is no maneuver to decapitate someone. The only way to decapitate a Werewolf in combat is to fill his health levels with aggravated damage, up to the last. Unless your players have a silver blade and some heavy dice pools, it is very hard to achieve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T16:49:50-08:00","id":806566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=806531#post806531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, so if a werewolf were to get shot in the head or something just as deadly to a human, while in most cases it would bring them up to full lethal, they could heal it in time if they have the Essence to do it. Alright, that makes sense, but what about decapitation? For starters, decapitating a monster to kill it is a common trope, so there's no narrative reason that it shouldn't work with werewolves (that I can see anyway). Second, it should also work on a logical level because even if a werewolf could regenerate full organs, I highly doubt they could do so in time, even with Essence.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, this is assuming that the decapitation is successful and I'm not really looking at the mechanics anymore, considering I was wrong about Killing Blows.</div> </div> </div> </div> Decapitating a werewolf will generally kill them, yes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T16:54:17-08:00","id":806570,"title":"","content":"If you're not ignoring the mechanics and you don't land enough damage for the instant kill, it may be useful to remember that decapitation sometimes takes a few hacks to get all the way through.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, people's necks are just that tough!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:39:10-08:00","id":806606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=806531#post806531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I thought Killing Blows did aggravated damage equal to the dice pool. Looks like I'm mistaken on that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically I think they do what ever kind of damage the weapon would normally deal. That usually means lethal, but if you're using your bare hands that would mean bashing and if you're using a silver weapon against a werewolf, that would mean aggravated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=806531#post806531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The narrative part of the question still stands, though. I mean, the 2E core has this to say on page 9: &quot;Silver is the best way to kill us, but it's not the only way. Sure, we heal really fast \u2014 but we need to get hurt to have something to heal from, and enough of that hurt will kill us as easily as it would anyone else.&quot;<br /> <br /> So clearly werewolves aren't invincible and are living creatures, so vital organ failure should be deadly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, definitely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=806531#post806531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so if a werewolf were to get shot in the head or something just as deadly to a human, while in most cases it would bring them up to full lethal, they could heal it in time if they have the Essence to do it. Alright, that makes sense, but what about decapitation? For starters, decapitating a monster to kill it is a common trope, so there's no narrative reason that it shouldn't work with werewolves (that I can see anyway). Second, it should also work on a logical level because even if a werewolf could regenerate full organs, I highly doubt they could do so in time, even with Essence.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, this is assuming that the decapitation is successful and I'm not really looking at the mechanics anymore, considering I was wrong about Killing Blows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, decapitation should work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T17:52:46-08:00","id":806619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=806531#post806531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what about decapitation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Decapitation isn't easy to achieve. Take a look at executions by beheading throughout history and it required a professional, with perfectly designed equipment and the best possible conditions to sever people's heads in a single swing. Even then they frequently failed. One of the reasons the Guillotine was such an amazing invention was that it could perform the same task with mechanical reliability.<br /> <br /> Without some very special effect in play, decapitation should almost always kill a werewolf. This doesn't require any special rules though, since the attempt to remove the head would inflict more than enough damage to completely fill the health track with aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T18:42:44-08:00","id":806654,"title":"","content":"Decapitation is pretty universally fatal even to werewolves. Though as another poster said, there's no default maneuver that lets you do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T18:30:23-08:00","id":812261,"title":"","content":"Despite what a lot of slasher flicks and zombie movies would have you believe, decapitation is not the easiest thing to achieve. Even guillotines didn't work perfectly every time. And that's just talking about human necks here. If the werewolf is in any other form, not only do you still have the flesh, muscle, and bone to deal with, you also have thick layers of fur (or just more muscle, in the case of <i>Dalu</i>). Fur is actually surprisingly effective as a sort of &quot;armor.&quot; Not enough to turn aside bullets or anything, of course, but it does make a noticeable difference.<br /> <br /> Werewolves can die of decapitation and organ failure. But to actually achieve these things, you need to do a ton of damage. Regeneration makes it very difficult to simply ambush a werewolf with a killing blow (to say nothing of their senses). You puncture a lung, the werewolf can regenerate it. Shred the heart and the werewolf goes down, but it's not instant, unless the damage is so severe that there's not enough of the werewolf left to regenerate (i.e., doing enough aggravated in a single attack to kill outright). Same with decapitation. You don't do enough damage to kill until you actually do enough damage to kill. There are no maneuvers for targeting the head or vitals and getting an insta-kill. You can't even do that and &quot;upgrade&quot; a lethal attack to aggravated damage, since werewolves explicitly take aggravated damage only directly from supernatural sources (and silver). Even if a Storyteller allows, say, a headshot to upgrade an attack's damage to aggravated on a human, to the werewolf it's &quot;only&quot; lethal. And they can heal lethal quickly.<br /> <br /> In 2E, werewolves are almost laughably hard to put down. They need to be. They hunt the most dangerous prey in the world: Humans. Spirits. Hosts. <i>Idigam</i>. Claimed. Other werewolves. And they tangle with other supernatural creatures. If you want to have a shot at killing a werewolf outright, bring an elephant gun. Or explosives. Or both. Drop a boulder on their head (though how you could manage that in secrecy I don't know). Otherwise, there's always a chance they'll survive. Your sneaky killing blow might do enough damage to the werewolf that she can't ever heal enough in time to survive further attacks. Or she might shift to <i>Gauru </i>and go berserk, becoming even harder to put down.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T20:05:18-08:00","id":812337,"title":"","content":"Or you could just make the call as ST saying it's an instant kill. I mean while there isn't a rule for it specifically, if someone is in a position where they take something you feel should be an instant kill, such as having their head blown off, just have it be an instant kill, no dice roll necessary. If one of your players has a werewolf knocked out unconscious, regardless of form, and they put a shotgun to its head and pull the trigger I'd say you'd be well within your rights to just say it's dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T21:14:07-08:00","id":812369,"title":"","content":"You could... but a monster getting up after you were sure you shot it to death is a common enough trope in the inspirational media for the games, that I wouldn't do that for supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T21:31:08-08:00","id":812382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=812369#post812369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could... but a monster getting up after you were sure you shot it to death is a common enough trope in the inspirational media for the games, that I wouldn't do that for supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is fine. I'm just saying that I wouldn't fault or even think twice about someone who did. It would be a perfectly reasonable call imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T01:18:43-08:00","id":812438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/805450-how-do-werewolves-deal-with-killing-blows-2e?p=812261#post812261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to have a shot at killing a werewolf outright, bring an elephant gun. Or explosives. Or both. Drop a boulder on their head (though how you could manage that in secrecy I don't know).</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/gBKH3cj.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}